<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH COALITION AGREES ENERGY VAT RISE - MINISTRY.</title>
<headline>CZECH COALITION AGREES ENERGY VAT RISE - MINISTRY.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech industry and trade ministry on Friday said that the ruling coalition had agreed to raise the value added tax (VAT) on electricity and natural gas to 22 percent from five percent, effective July 1.</p>
<p>Ministry spokesman Miroslav Konvalina said that Industry Minister Vladimir Dlouhy had confirmed the agreement following a meeting of leaders of the coalition on Thursday, although ministers said after the meeting that there was not yet a final agreement on the VAT rise.</p>
</text>
